FlintTrade is a native-first trading platform: its backend, native gateway
contract, safety/gating layer, and the bulk of its application code are
original work by the FlintTrade authors. It is not a fork of another trading
application, and it can interoperate with OpenAlgo through an optional bridge
adapter rather than bundling OpenAlgo's source.

A number of widgets and modules were adapted from open-source projects. Where a
file was adapted from a specific upstream source it carries an in-source
"Absorbed from:" header naming that source; the licence terms and attribution of
those upstream projects are preserved here. (Reducing this adapted surface to
fully-original implementations is in progress.)

